WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:01.903
(audience applauding)

2
00:00:01.903 --> 00:00:03.180
Hi, Lonnie.

3
00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.500
Hi, Ms. Drew.
(chuckling)

4
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.563
How are you?

5
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.153
I'm doing fine how about you?

6
00:00:10.153 --> 00:00:11.514
I mean, it's the morning, I don't really like mornings

7
00:00:11.514 --> 00:00:13.382
but I'm happy to be alive.

8
00:00:13.382 --> 00:00:14.660
I'm grateful to be here.

9
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.437
That's literally, how old are you?

10
00:00:17.437 --> 00:00:18.610
I'm 13 years old.

11
00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:21.267
That's exactly where you're supposed to be.

12
00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:23.696
(laughing)

13
00:00:23.696 --> 00:00:25.020
I hated mornings too.

14
00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.980
I think until I was 30 in my late thirties, actually.

15
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.980
And you know, you learn a lot along the way,

16
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.342
and it sounds like, Lonnie,

17
00:00:36.342 --> 00:00:38.680
that you learned a lot from David working on this film.

18
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.597
Will you tell me about that?

19
00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.970
Well, first I want to say you'd think it would be hard

20
00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.550 line:15%
for someone who's not only an actor and a director

21
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.174 line:15%
of a movie, especially on their first director debut.

22
00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:50.530
(snapping)
Mr. David.

23
00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.930
Because of how many things they have to control.

24
00:00:53.856 --> 00:00:55.910
But Mr. David never bumped a transition.

25
00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.910
I mean, he made it look like a walk in the park

26
00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.383
throughout the whole entire set of the movie.

27
00:01:01.383 --> 00:01:03.030
And honestly, it was such,

28
00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.650
it was such a pleasure to work with him.

29
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.070
I feel so grateful.

30
00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:09.260
I have to say Lonnie, I was looking into

31
00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:13.594
your anti-bullying campaign, Fix Your Heart.

32
00:01:13.594 --> 00:01:15.450
And I was wondering if you would talk about it

33
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.750
because I am so swept away with it.

34
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.433
And I would love to hear you explain why you started this.

35
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:29.240
Sure, well, Fix Your Heart is an anti-bullying campaign

36
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.180
that I created with my mom after being told

37
00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:34.000
online and offline that I needed to fix my gap

38
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.440
that I had in my teeth.

39
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.470
And I said, braces can fix this,

40
00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.520
but can you fix your heart though?

41
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.280
So we created Fix Your Heart TV,

42
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.010
where I bring on people to talk about their experiences

43
00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.800
and hopefully change other people's perspectives

44
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.620
to be kinder people.

45
00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.580
And we created a clothing line because I love fashion,

46
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.100
and part of the proceeds goes back to Fix Your Heart TV

47
00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.910 line:15%
and other inspired charities that I believe in.

48
00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.739 line:15%
Do you mean this?

49
00:01:58.739 --> 00:02:00.457 line:15%
Because I'm holding it because I got a box.

50
00:02:00.457 --> 00:02:01.525 line:15%
Oh, you have one.

51
00:02:01.525 --> 00:02:04.490
Yeah, I got a box of swag

52
00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:08.270
and I want to wear it so proudly.

53
00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:13.045
I have to tell you, I'm not kidding, I love the message

54
00:02:13.045 --> 00:02:16.760
of this so much and I want to share it with my kids.

55
00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:19.870
And I just love your Fix Your Heart TV.

56
00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.480
You interview people about being kind

57
00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.620
and David you know, is it, would it be okay

58
00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:32.270
if you quickly interviewed Lonnie and I both right now

59
00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:35.950
for Fix Your Heart TV, would you be up for that?

60
00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.020
Yes, absolutely.

61
00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.360
I've got some prepared questions here.

62
00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:39.630
Okay, perfect.

63
00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:43.450
When you realize you've hurt someone by your actions,

64
00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.723
how do you fix your heart?

65
00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:49.310
Well, the whole purpose and the whole definition

66
00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.300
of Fix Your Heart is to have the accountability

67
00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.354
to correct your own actions and be better to others,

68
00:02:55.354 --> 00:02:57.210
and maybe sometimes just yourself.

69
00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.940
I mean, how do I fix my own heart?

70
00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:02.537
Have the accountability to say sorry, a hundred percent.

71
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.710
I feel like that is probably where

72
00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.163
I hold myself the most accountable.

73
00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:16.550
I wish I had half, a quarter, 1% of the concern for myself

74
00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.120
that I do for others,

75
00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:23.668
which is probably a good start and maybe enough sometimes.

76
00:03:23.668 --> 00:03:27.023
But if I ever do things that I think don't feel right,

77
00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.750
I really hold myself accountable.

78
00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.020
Lonnie, would you like to extend

79
00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.443
the same questions to David, if you don't mind?

80
00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.610
Oh, a hundred percent.

81
00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:39.443
Let's go.

82
00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:44.869
Well now you have both been in the business

83
00:03:44.869 --> 00:03:48.520
before the time of social media, unlike me,

84
00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:53.500
and social media has given canceling people a whole culture.

85
00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.240
Making mistakes are inevitable though,

86
00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.853
because we are human, of course.

87
00:03:57.845 --> 00:04:00.130
So Ms. Drew, do you worry about making a mistake

88
00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.663
and being canceled?

89
00:04:05.145 --> 00:04:08.210
Yeah, I never want to say things

90
00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:10.889
or do things that hurts anybody,

91
00:04:10.889 --> 00:04:14.140
because it's the last thing on earth I want to do.

92
00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:16.330
I don't want to affect other people negatively.

93
00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.763
David, what do you think?

94
00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.713
Gosh, it's a really great question.

95
00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:27.120
I mean, first and foremost, I do try to live by

96
00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.423
treat each others as you would like to be treated.

97
00:04:31.532 --> 00:04:34.490
And so, to have compassion, to have kindness,

98
00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:39.490
to have empathy is the way to lead, to understand.

99
00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:44.193
And for me personally, as a black person especially,

100
00:04:45.976 --> 00:04:50.976
I know what it feels like to be willfully misunderstood,

101
00:04:52.097 --> 00:04:55.780
mistreated, marginalized.

102
00:04:55.780 --> 00:05:00.313
And so I absolutely refuse to do that to another person.

103
00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:04.100
I think, love, the definition of love

104
00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.223
is to put others before yourself.

105
00:05:07.319 --> 00:05:08.970
And if you're doing that, I think there's a real chance

106
00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.020
that you won't go hurting anyone.

107
00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:12.620
Certainly not knowingly, anyway.

108
00:05:13.974 --> 00:05:16.800
I love hearing that and Lonnie,

109
00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.600 line:15%
I want to thank you for coming on this show

110
00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.390 line:15%
and allowing our show to jump into

111
00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:26.400 line:15%
Fix Your Heart TV with David,

112
00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:30.540
because when I saw it and was pouring through it

113
00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:33.284
I just fell in love with your mission.

114
00:05:33.284 --> 00:05:34.434
Thank you, thank you for having

115
00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:35.763
Fix Your Heart TV on your show.

116
00:05:35.763 --> 00:05:37.145
It really means a lot to me.

117
00:05:37.145 --> 00:05:38.088
Thank you.

118
00:05:38.088 --> 00:05:40.638
And most importantly, to speak about your beautiful

119
00:05:41.879 --> 00:05:43.870
feature directorial debut

120
00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:45.860
and this gorgeous story that you're telling

121
00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:50.110
in The Water Man, David Oyelowo and Lonnie Chavis.

122
00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.820
Thank you for bringing The Water Man,

123
00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.100
which is in theaters right now,

124
00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:58.350
to all of us, and asking the questions that you asked.

125
00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.300
Thank you.

126
00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.470
Thanks for having us, Drew.

127
00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:01.810
Thank you so much.

128
00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.304
Thank you, I appreciate it so much, thank you.

129
00:06:03.304 --> 00:06:05.887 line:15%
(upbeat music)

